Apply order 0034 against mariopartyrd/partyboard 98ac07fd1e8f7ab938bbb6fe75789fad99419010 (CC0-1.0; ADR 0009 section 5).
lottery: the COM's crank input stays on its last entry instead of reading past the table, on MPT_PC
Applied in order by runtimes/gc_wii/mp4/CMakeLists.txt with `git apply`.

M4-03, found by reading while the board sweep's lottery soft locks were diagnosed; it is not their
cause (that was the human seat's handle, which the test autopilot never turned: docs/titles/mp4.md,
M4-03). In the lottery's ball game (ExecBallGame, game/board/lottery.c) a COM player turns the
handle from comInputBall, one stick position per frame, with comInputPos (a u8) advanced every frame
until the handle reaches its end. The table ends with { 0x7F, 0x7F }, which marks the COM done, but
nothing stops the index there: while the handle is still short of its end, it runs on past the
terminator and reads whatever follows the table in memory, which on PC is other module data that the
linker is free to place there. Those bytes then drive the handle (a still or repeated sample slows
it by 7% a frame, and a slowed handle may never reach its end). The index now stays on the
terminator, so the COM's last turn speed is kept and the handle runs to its end. Unconditional on
PC. No synthetic test: the function is static and needs the whole board to run; the board sweep
covers it.

diff --git a/src/game/board/lottery.c b/src/game/board/lottery.c
index 08ddde0..7dcc77e 100755
--- a/src/game/board/lottery.c
+++ b/src/game/board/lottery.c
@@ -868,7 +868,18 @@ static void ExecBallGame(void)
                 spA = HuPadStkY[temp_r25];
             }
             else {
+#ifdef MPT_PC
+                /* The COM's crank input ends at { 0x7F, 0x7F } ("done"), but comInputPos ran on past it
+                 * every frame until the handle reached its end, reading whatever followed the table:
+                 * other module data on PC, placed by the linker, which then drove the handle. It stays
+                 * on the last entry instead, which keeps the handle's speed until it reaches its end. */
+                temp_r23 = comInputBall[comInputPos];
+                if (comInputPos < sizeof(comInputBall) / sizeof(comInputBall[0]) - 1) {
+                    comInputPos++;
+                }
+#else
                 temp_r23 = comInputBall[comInputPos++];
+#endif
                 spB = temp_r23[0];
                 spA = temp_r23[1];
             }
